# The Temple Premium: Fact or Folklore?

While I didn't inlcude the datasets in this repository due to the size and licensing, here are the links were I obtained them:

- **Temple Announcements and Dedications**: [3rd party website called churchofjesuschristtemples.org](https://churchofjesuschristtemples.org/statistics/timelines/)
- **Demographic and Socioeconomic Data**: accessed via the [tidycensus R package](https://walker-data.com/tidycensus/) in the code.
- **Real Estate Data**: [Zillow Research Data](https://www.zillow.com/research/data/). I used the "Zillow Home Value Index (ZHVI)" dataset at the zipcode level.
- **Religion Census Data**: [Association of Religion Data Archives (ARDA)](https://www.thearda.com/data-archive?fid=RCMSCY10)

You can run through the code sequentially in the 3 R scripts. Each script is standalone, independent, and contains comments to guide you through the process. The scripts are:

1_eda.r: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and initial tables used in some visualization.
2_modeling.r: The core difference-in-differences modeling code.
3_statistical_checks.r: Additional statistical checks and robustness tests.

Please don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or need further assistance. Contact me at alex@bassempirical.com Thanks for caring about this analysis enough to make it this far!